<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>All minimum T-bill prices fell at Monday's primary tender after investors bid for 689 million zlotys of the bills against a one billion zloty offer, the National Bank of Poland said.  </p>
<p>    T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week 52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     95.46    91.12	--     83.48</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.48)  (91.13)     --    (83.50)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.52    91.17	--     83.70</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.55)  (91.17)     --    (83.80)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     250.0    250.0	--     500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --     147.1    114.8	--     427.2</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --     147.1    110.8	--     404.2</p>
<p>   next auction	--     300.0    200.0	--     600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
